{
"dur": 52.019,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 4.822,
"text": "Then in 1986, it went wrong in a way most people wouldn't expect.",
"end": 5.097
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 5.097,
"vo_start": 5.372,
"vo_end": 14.372,
"text": "The danger everyone watched for was homeowners who stopped paying. Fink's problem was the opposite. Rates fell, and homeowners paid back early.",
"end": 14.647
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 14.647,
"vo_start": 14.922,
"vo_end": 21.602,
"text": "Picture a family with a two hundred thousand dollar loan at nine percent. Their payment is about sixteen hundred dollars a month for thirty years.",
"end": 21.877
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 21.877,
"vo_start": 22.152,
"vo_end": 27.232,
"text": "When a bank down the road offers seven percent, they take a new loan, pay off the old one, and walk out.",
"end": 27.507
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 27.507,
"vo_start": 27.782,
"vo_end": 31.742,
"text": "For whoever owned that old loan, thirty years of nine percent interest simply disappears.",
"end": 32.017
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 32.017,
"vo_start": 32.292,
"vo_end": 37.532,
"text": "Fink's desk had bet the wrong way on rates. It lost about a hundred million dollars.",
"end": 37.807
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 37.807,
"vo_start": 38.082,
"vo_end": 43.362,
"text": "The star became the man who lost a hundred million. Within two years, he left First Boston.",
"end": 43.637
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 43.637,
"vo_start": 43.912,
"vo_end": 51.069,
"text": "He later said the lesson was simple. His team had been brilliant at making money and had no real idea how much risk it was carrying.",
"end": 52.019
}
],
